[{:db/id "q-353456/field-1/aa4e4239377eb61b8bdf37e9f4374abeb3a1fdeaaf409dc6e37519ad01509799" :answer/id #uuid "0c159438-6e95-51e6-b234-a97c0f88923b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353456/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "55562101-d926-57a6-9d9a-11e91e78dd61" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353456/field-1/aa4e4239377eb61b8bdf37e9f4374abeb3a1fdeaaf409dc6e37519ad01509799" :answer-field/choices ["q-353456/field-1/aa4e4239377eb61b8bdf37e9f4374abeb3a1fdeaaf409dc6e37519ad01509799"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353456" :question/id #uuid "aee119a0-6724-5f1a-853e-70adb75e75c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-353456" :question/problem "A bookstore sells $27$ copies of a particular novel every day. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the number of copies $N(t)$ remaining in stock? Assume that the time $t$ is measured in days.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=$  \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If the number of copies remaining in stock is $N,$ then the rate of change of the number of copies is $\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in days.\n\nSince $27$ copies are sold each day, the rate of change of the number of copies is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=-27.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is negative because the number of copies remaining is *decreasing*." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-353456/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a247a205-ca5c-5079-820c-cfa34b6f53db"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353456"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119052/selection/1e630281fa9677b0fec8355ffecf1103364055f1fb6b1b435d111b721322a0bf" :answer/id #uuid "fa86354b-b7d0-5914-b45a-4ca47137e0f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119052/selection/e04109b3b44027f5fd6c659cab8f4b663465e395d9830506892b231f699b4195" :answer/id #uuid "799bfcb6-3708-5802-9f4a-57f4cb9791ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-5S" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119052/selection/58673bf278bd0aa3683dd608870fdd90edf9b07451cb0773655c08920cfe8659" :answer/id #uuid "a035a897-48f4-559e-91de-9a87d4030048" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119052/selection/2595b7430da564ab26551d801232aa147b090de31402b41052d622056d1318c3" :answer/id #uuid "51eff358-2390-532f-98da-b66e94258aaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-5t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119052/selection/19fb41de198f04a8feec1f4d6a29721acc677518f61e107ee5cfdff8e0256ed1" :answer/id #uuid "452ce28e-0228-58ef-abad-de2089e6ffe6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119052/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "94ea4618-9dc5-548a-b85a-b4f9a69dc59f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-119052/selection/1e630281fa9677b0fec8355ffecf1103364055f1fb6b1b435d111b721322a0bf" :answer-field/choices ["q-119052/selection/1e630281fa9677b0fec8355ffecf1103364055f1fb6b1b435d111b721322a0bf" "q-119052/selection/e04109b3b44027f5fd6c659cab8f4b663465e395d9830506892b231f699b4195" "q-119052/selection/58673bf278bd0aa3683dd608870fdd90edf9b07451cb0773655c08920cfe8659" "q-119052/selection/2595b7430da564ab26551d801232aa147b090de31402b41052d622056d1318c3" "q-119052/selection/19fb41de198f04a8feec1f4d6a29721acc677518f61e107ee5cfdff8e0256ed1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119052" :question/id #uuid "1f1906d2-5133-52e7-99dc-75f54ead86d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-119052" :question/problem "Tommy drinks $5$ milliliters of vitamin syrup each day from a bottle. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the amount of vitamin syrup $S$ (in milliliters) remaining in the bottle? Assume that the time $t$ is measured in days." :question/worked-solution "If the amount of vitamin syrup remaining is $S$ milliliters, then the rate of change of the syrup volume is $\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in days.\n\nSince Tommy drinks $5$ milliliters of syrup each day, the rate of change of the amount of syrup remaining is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-5.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is negative because the amount of syrup is *decreasing*." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-119052/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a247a205-ca5c-5079-820c-cfa34b6f53db"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119052"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79304/selection/5e426550980d6d2c73dbaad28092666e2f57b6d31252e51f3c02d99bf2cfd419" :answer/id #uuid "b44a8375-242c-5d00-ae4d-829c72ace46f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t}=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79304/selection/b1f33d217cbe9f12c69844d1e43a31602e2d8a071dac4385c083540c0f736275" :answer/id #uuid "0d855636-3364-5d8b-aa8b-421b77091170" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t}=2Wt" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79304/selection/e502f21af72b9c1ee5f9a3bc2de48dd96a66fa7caa0369073e0df33a930d0a91" :answer/id #uuid "43879884-d223-5b7d-80bb-18654f38bb9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t}=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79304/selection/f522b28daaaf521b50d89be7aab8e19434a5cdd519b4fe8fc794f8504240da63" :answer/id #uuid "a17acce0-aa71-5ca1-8549-62558ff3ffd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t}={e}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79304/selection/e04420e9b5518ea56fcc96b97069eb5da6aaed5cae7419197d9e3bda8e46accd" :answer/id #uuid "430f0556-ee1a-5fd9-9093-ac8dd2252148" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t}=-2W" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79304/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "22758b37-2407-5d75-9819-e74aa4c9e3a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79304/selection/e502f21af72b9c1ee5f9a3bc2de48dd96a66fa7caa0369073e0df33a930d0a91" :answer-field/choices ["q-79304/selection/5e426550980d6d2c73dbaad28092666e2f57b6d31252e51f3c02d99bf2cfd419" "q-79304/selection/b1f33d217cbe9f12c69844d1e43a31602e2d8a071dac4385c083540c0f736275" "q-79304/selection/e502f21af72b9c1ee5f9a3bc2de48dd96a66fa7caa0369073e0df33a930d0a91" "q-79304/selection/f522b28daaaf521b50d89be7aab8e19434a5cdd519b4fe8fc794f8504240da63" "q-79304/selection/e04420e9b5518ea56fcc96b97069eb5da6aaed5cae7419197d9e3bda8e46accd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79304" :question/id #uuid "3b4ccbf6-ff25-5987-a288-2f0b9f57a5f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-79304" :question/problem "A total of $2$ milliliters of water evaporate from a beaker every second.\nWhat differential equation describes the rate of change of the amount of water $W$ (in milliliters) remaining in the beaker?  Assume that the time $t$ is measured in seconds." :question/worked-solution "If the amount of water in the beaker is $W$ milliliters, then the rate of change of the amount of water is $\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in seconds.\n\nSince $2$ milliliters of water are lost every second, the rate of change of the amount of water is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t}=-2.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is negative because the beaker is losing water." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79304/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a247a205-ca5c-5079-820c-cfa34b6f53db"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79304"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353450/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "7dd7f633-7e4d-5821-8932-39f8b0f9c7d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353450/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f9084464-638e-5383-8eff-c53bd8138371" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353450/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-353450/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353450" :question/id #uuid "e6c359cf-143f-56b3-afa9-7065f4bc4406" :question/math-academy-id "q-353450" :question/problem "The distance traveled by a conveyor belt increases by $5$ meters every minute while it operates at a constant speed. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the distance traveled $X(t)?$ Assume that the time $t$ is measured in minutes.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}X}{\\text{d}t}=$  \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If the distance traveled is $X,$ then the rate of change of the distance traveled is $\\frac{\\text{d}X}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in minutes.\n\nSince the conveyor belt moves $5$ meters every minute, the rate of change of the distance traveled is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}X}{\\text{d}t}=5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-353450/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a247a205-ca5c-5079-820c-cfa34b6f53db"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353450"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79315/selection/e66168866a59358e6c6361c7c54c5e5a5a001dbe968feb56362fc9ee1a3ebda4" :answer/id #uuid "b6711347-e1d4-5280-b4df-46f5b6c665f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{D},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79315/selection/e5314c692e477ba4d90e349d0bdca8a115c156883421f1ec9bf0e4f9724d857f" :answer/id #uuid "8cff1f96-e519-5093-86d9-c1dd85c770bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{t},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79315/selection/8d1d9b7fedceeccb52648532ca30ce60b1b07630b6b48b5c5b9fd032654591ea" :answer/id #uuid "79fe879d-f28b-532b-91fa-75acf55fef00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{kt}{D},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79315/selection/411451d6cccd2bdde63bb534899ef10cc54346a08b5f31ba29ba4fac24287a57" :answer/id #uuid "a569ad01-7e3f-5741-8664-40ce66f4e6e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=kt,\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79315/selection/8bec02f8a05fa8cd203554251217199f2437cd5ace927aa3d8b3aa950e224eb4" :answer/id #uuid "2441ff52-edca-57e8-82ec-a678a61869b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=kD,\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79315/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f666668e-e567-53d1-9f1d-58b12fed78f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79315/selection/411451d6cccd2bdde63bb534899ef10cc54346a08b5f31ba29ba4fac24287a57" :answer-field/choices ["q-79315/selection/e66168866a59358e6c6361c7c54c5e5a5a001dbe968feb56362fc9ee1a3ebda4" "q-79315/selection/e5314c692e477ba4d90e349d0bdca8a115c156883421f1ec9bf0e4f9724d857f" "q-79315/selection/8d1d9b7fedceeccb52648532ca30ce60b1b07630b6b48b5c5b9fd032654591ea" "q-79315/selection/411451d6cccd2bdde63bb534899ef10cc54346a08b5f31ba29ba4fac24287a57" "q-79315/selection/8bec02f8a05fa8cd203554251217199f2437cd5ace927aa3d8b3aa950e224eb4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79315" :question/id #uuid "ba66d242-26a0-594d-82a7-1f167d592d18" :question/math-academy-id "q-79315" :question/problem "The rate of growth of a car's displacement increases at a rate that's proportional to the time $t$ since the car started moving. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the car's displacement, $D,$ at time $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The rate of growth of a **car's displacement** $D(t)$ **increases** at a **rate** that's **proportional** to the **time** $t$ since the car started moving.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *car's displacement* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *interval of time* since the car started moving. In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}∝t.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the car's displacement *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=kt.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-79315/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "255dee12-5f44-536b-b679-5a894843395d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79315"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-38588/selection/63cd8a0d9c120877e934886f7096ca497a597215a8eb348fb44a15cd14f35708" :answer/id #uuid "d3fc1e2a-d7b9-55f3-a8db-4948caf4a01d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=tA" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38588/selection/a7ade859dca3b1387955e6007862c27c72c2d5b89bd73bc46c99ec47d2d6928a" :answer/id #uuid "447c66c6-c98e-5588-85c8-7e7329e54077" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=k-A,\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38588/selection/f26152a05ad807a4d4a78eb3780b02a262e0feeba8f15691e7549eab3f88e7a4" :answer/id #uuid "26ae4d63-2052-5085-b656-7698d7989d9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=kA,\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38588/selection/77f218f6ca0f1f0572165140853e069a445dd149f7ccfe831b60ce703a82db97" :answer/id #uuid "ee7dacc6-1e01-5aed-9065-745a0c1b937c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38588/selection/7bdf37cd1446c0c28e233267f06e9a3d5b288ee0de8fe6dffec7282071695428" :answer/id #uuid "67be357a-be3d-5b48-8131-6c31c67bb821" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=k+A,\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38588/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5ebaaa1d-ab07-54c5-a725-cf8b3eccfce2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-38588/selection/f26152a05ad807a4d4a78eb3780b02a262e0feeba8f15691e7549eab3f88e7a4" :answer-field/choices ["q-38588/selection/63cd8a0d9c120877e934886f7096ca497a597215a8eb348fb44a15cd14f35708" "q-38588/selection/a7ade859dca3b1387955e6007862c27c72c2d5b89bd73bc46c99ec47d2d6928a" "q-38588/selection/f26152a05ad807a4d4a78eb3780b02a262e0feeba8f15691e7549eab3f88e7a4" "q-38588/selection/77f218f6ca0f1f0572165140853e069a445dd149f7ccfe831b60ce703a82db97" "q-38588/selection/7bdf37cd1446c0c28e233267f06e9a3d5b288ee0de8fe6dffec7282071695428"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-38588" :question/id #uuid "6e3c5c93-86d8-5789-925d-7bd84acb1b9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-38588" :question/problem "The number of ants in an anthill increases at a rate that is proportional to the number of ants at the moment. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the number of ants, $A,$ at time $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **number of ants** in an anthill **increases** at a **rate** that is **proportional** to the **number of ants** at the moment.* \n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *number of ants* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *number of ants.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}∝A.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the number of ants *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=kA.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-38588/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "255dee12-5f44-536b-b679-5a894843395d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38588"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-38310"] :question/problem "For the first year of a newborn's life, its height $H$ increases at a rate that is proportional to the time, in months, since birth.\nWhat differential equation describes the rate of change of the height of the baby at time $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*For the first year of a newborn's life, its **height** $H$ **increases** at a **rate** that is **proportional** to the **time**, in months, since birth.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *height* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *time* since birth. In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}∝t.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the height *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=kt.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-143036/selection/5536274e6cb969a1e5dcc7f6b2d0c8aeaca873915f3b452bbd445a6b0c37d6a0" :answer/id #uuid "9188262e-9673-5eed-83b2-a5fd5cd3b6d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=k{v}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143036/selection/dba251b0566af11970278e51bc1d2f02a932476f80843921a9b667a7352c1c01" :answer/id #uuid "114d7be1-1926-558d-8724-31e887cac167" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{{v}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143036/selection/5177a679b071430b40569a896474c0d3f78d1deb0e6f38101243a12d569e1765" :answer/id #uuid "63a1febe-6a7a-5422-8c17-c5540c2e7e97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=-k{v}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143036/selection/41112d6bec5b159cfbd468653670970883564f072fae187bfb6c633914499617" :answer/id #uuid "6a4c60a8-f101-5eef-9c93-587751322eb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=k\\sqrt{v},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143036/selection/96be9988a69f2223004164fcf6c6ce57a24c95577ef812f81d3fb092ff1478ef" :answer/id #uuid "7f71007e-d2c5-54ea-bfc6-348221a38aa4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{v}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143036/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "27ffd44f-d95c-5b66-9de7-8b47da4773de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143036/selection/5177a679b071430b40569a896474c0d3f78d1deb0e6f38101243a12d569e1765" :answer-field/choices ["q-143036/selection/5536274e6cb969a1e5dcc7f6b2d0c8aeaca873915f3b452bbd445a6b0c37d6a0" "q-143036/selection/dba251b0566af11970278e51bc1d2f02a932476f80843921a9b667a7352c1c01" "q-143036/selection/5177a679b071430b40569a896474c0d3f78d1deb0e6f38101243a12d569e1765" "q-143036/selection/41112d6bec5b159cfbd468653670970883564f072fae187bfb6c633914499617" "q-143036/selection/96be9988a69f2223004164fcf6c6ce57a24c95577ef812f81d3fb092ff1478ef"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143036" :question/id #uuid "000bf12e-faf9-50f0-869d-67748f8e8824" :question/math-academy-id "q-143036" :question/problem "The velocity $v$ of a stone falling through some water to the bottom of a lake decreases with time. The rate of change of the stone's velocity is proportional to the square of the velocity. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the velocity at time $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **velocity** $v$ of a stone falling through some water to the bottom of a lake **decreases** with time. The **rate** of change of the stone's velocity is **proportional** to the **square of the velocity**.  *\n\nWe note the following: \n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *velocity* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *velocity squared.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}∝{v}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the velocity *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=-k{v}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-143036/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "344f1838-a027-5fd5-82da-17e9b4fcac2b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143036"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143035/selection/1fb8546af3a650636ff65e964f7053d925bb71fe26182eefa4b3b4138beea202" :answer/id #uuid "68b74365-7af7-533c-a4b6-82b95ad8c598" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143035/selection/d50c07fc53710803ec40f6c4fb5850559c8ffed9bfb0c0e1d23e46e4304aaaf3" :answer/id #uuid "3e965958-eaee-5339-9cf7-a5c18c0224a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143035/selection/3e3342254778d59d60635fd4ddba98c8b80e26c2c23b30ac84f11d13b092b7b3" :answer/id #uuid "4dac0845-ece5-5c93-ac78-e3107df5c303" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}=-k{t}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143035/selection/742c8d453f0f1505f66a5cdc9e0ee194a40ca477be39da8a2ced0b9faa11fde6" :answer/id #uuid "978ca961-fc0f-5ab9-9bc4-26f6aa707375" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}=k{t}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143035/selection/8228176286074bfa4179d0082e9b79a857d5fcfb78a263e2a853b072f1926341" :answer/id #uuid "b49dba43-1fc2-53b2-b7f9-3b4142fab53c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}=-kt,\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143035/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b79b0e9e-ce07-5367-ae03-a5fb5855bf88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143035/selection/742c8d453f0f1505f66a5cdc9e0ee194a40ca477be39da8a2ced0b9faa11fde6" :answer-field/choices ["q-143035/selection/1fb8546af3a650636ff65e964f7053d925bb71fe26182eefa4b3b4138beea202" "q-143035/selection/d50c07fc53710803ec40f6c4fb5850559c8ffed9bfb0c0e1d23e46e4304aaaf3" "q-143035/selection/3e3342254778d59d60635fd4ddba98c8b80e26c2c23b30ac84f11d13b092b7b3" "q-143035/selection/742c8d453f0f1505f66a5cdc9e0ee194a40ca477be39da8a2ced0b9faa11fde6" "q-143035/selection/8228176286074bfa4179d0082e9b79a857d5fcfb78a263e2a853b072f1926341"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143035" :question/id #uuid "116a80ae-5b7a-5a13-919a-314322a246f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-143035" :question/problem "During a certain chemical reaction, the volume of gas $G$ increases with time. The rate of change of the volume of gas is proportional to the square of the time $t,$ in seconds, since the reaction started. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the volume of gas at time $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*During a certain chemical reaction, the **volume** of gas $G$ **increases** with time. The **rate** of change of the volume of gas is **proportional** to the **square of the time** $t,$ in seconds.  *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *volume of gas* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *square of the time.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}∝{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the volume of gas *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}=k{t}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-143035/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "344f1838-a027-5fd5-82da-17e9b4fcac2b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143035"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143058/selection/3bb240da68f371aa593e395b493da7d7debbf467c98e7162f3c06b8563329112" :answer/id #uuid "0cb91c8b-41a8-5201-a728-dda49efb372f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=kH,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143058/selection/1abb5661b04dff5a888c3ed9624b548dcf51862b728edf78bad07f0b063a11ea" :answer/id #uuid "08fff3d5-f006-5e51-b487-252567288d43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-kH,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143058/selection/89ef2d9b1b78a5026376e36f7747fec5114bfdcef2cbf7b359a11ed20bc2d4c1" :answer/id #uuid "d0e1903b-8dd1-5d3e-990b-7e0192bf2bf9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{t},\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143058/selection/ea1a67997be603982295394b0a2944156b26559e15fc5116feced390f7156acf" :answer/id #uuid "ce285e3c-2f8f-5986-9c6a-2c74be616204" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{H},\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143058/selection/0834e3df7163b6c32fb0e1065f7acbba11b602b993887cdaa096c0a7f9cb985f" :answer/id #uuid "aefdcf67-bcdc-5ed9-b0c0-b392a37658bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{H},\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143058/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9392e9a-f656-5daf-b678-018e74b9f8bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143058/selection/0834e3df7163b6c32fb0e1065f7acbba11b602b993887cdaa096c0a7f9cb985f" :answer-field/choices ["q-143058/selection/3bb240da68f371aa593e395b493da7d7debbf467c98e7162f3c06b8563329112" "q-143058/selection/1abb5661b04dff5a888c3ed9624b548dcf51862b728edf78bad07f0b063a11ea" "q-143058/selection/89ef2d9b1b78a5026376e36f7747fec5114bfdcef2cbf7b359a11ed20bc2d4c1" "q-143058/selection/ea1a67997be603982295394b0a2944156b26559e15fc5116feced390f7156acf" "q-143058/selection/0834e3df7163b6c32fb0e1065f7acbba11b602b993887cdaa096c0a7f9cb985f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143058" :question/id #uuid "91ea1276-29dd-5d34-8bf4-312e105d7100" :question/math-academy-id "q-143058" :question/problem "The height $H$ of a tree increases at a rate that's inversely proportional to the tree's height at that moment.\nWhat differential equation describes the rate of change of the height $H?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **height** $H$ of a tree **increases** at a rate that's **inversely proportional** to the **tree's height** $H$ at that moment. *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *height* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}$ is *inversely proportional to* the *tree's height.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}∝\\frac{1}{H}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the height *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{H}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-143058/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d6e417b-e2a7-57f1-8dcd-4de5ff5d7e6b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143058"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79306/selection/d93ccd67c2bb2db414d795dbb94ba14fe4060793018382a1d07ade44476a9b74" :answer/id #uuid "d710dcda-1285-5da2-a72a-eeb9cade0226" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k{T}^{3},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79306/selection/622f0142143ac893ade46203eb8a8875859f8e3a7fe037e0ec8fa3c85dd01e81" :answer/id #uuid "d276e2bc-ab90-53f5-a791-7402cee1af46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=k\\sqrt[3]{T},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79306/selection/32ccb06a16c2387fe84c783b2c90f0b1cdc27e127ca766223e8f7cca9081618a" :answer/id #uuid "986154db-dfac-5a07-82eb-311209aa0418" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=k{T}^{3},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79306/selection/bd38e9f227ef2eabdb804609b1884bf6b3a2013193ce9c2f0e118806b9fe0530" :answer/id #uuid "c0a98ea7-6b9a-5569-94ba-43f3cdb94373" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{{T}^{3}},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79306/selection/f17007f8ee57ae38308839f5a563f5e7bf565e4e4688e67436c02b8b7eb18e7e" :answer/id #uuid "2400aa9d-14e3-5ce3-96d5-a7082bb62e01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{\\sqrt[3]{T}},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79306/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b73c3167-d9bd-5f62-9aac-daf335b92dfd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79306/selection/bd38e9f227ef2eabdb804609b1884bf6b3a2013193ce9c2f0e118806b9fe0530" :answer-field/choices ["q-79306/selection/d93ccd67c2bb2db414d795dbb94ba14fe4060793018382a1d07ade44476a9b74" "q-79306/selection/622f0142143ac893ade46203eb8a8875859f8e3a7fe037e0ec8fa3c85dd01e81" "q-79306/selection/32ccb06a16c2387fe84c783b2c90f0b1cdc27e127ca766223e8f7cca9081618a" "q-79306/selection/bd38e9f227ef2eabdb804609b1884bf6b3a2013193ce9c2f0e118806b9fe0530" "q-79306/selection/f17007f8ee57ae38308839f5a563f5e7bf565e4e4688e67436c02b8b7eb18e7e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79306" :question/id #uuid "e640b0e6-4f4b-5358-84ca-251a991cee48" :question/math-academy-id "q-79306" :question/problem "In a controlled environment, the temperature $T$ of a hot drink decreases at a rate that's inversely proportional to the cube of the temperature. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the temperature of the drink $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*In a controlled environment, the **temperature** $T$ of a hot drink **decreases** at a rate that's **inversely proportional** to the **cube of the temperature** $T.$*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *temperature* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}$ is *inversely proportional to* the *cube of the temperature.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}∝\\frac{1}{{T}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the temperature *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{{T}^{3}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79306/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d6e417b-e2a7-57f1-8dcd-4de5ff5d7e6b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79306"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
